# Planned ON a 5560U INSIDE the Sigmond Proxmox VM (AI6VN-PM, VM 100:
# 10 vCPUs pinned 1:1 to host CPUs 0-9, 13 GiB), on radiod's own core
# (vCPU 6 = host pCPU 6) with the host laid out for TWO radiods: pCPUs
# 6-9 pinned at the production 3.2 GHz, in the resctrl "radiod" group
# (L3:0=3ff, 10 of 16 ways = 5 MiB), workers 0-5 at 1.4 GHz.  Made with
# `smd admin wisdom plan --fresh` (fftwf-wisdom -n): all 65 profiles
# measured here, nothing imported.  Run time 1 h 59 m (2026-10-31
# 23:04Z - 2026-11-01 01:03Z), station stopped throughout.
#
# Supersedes two earlier attempts the same day: a non-fresh run that
# imported the WB6CXC-7 bundle, and a fresh run measured while pCPU 6
# was still a 1.4 GHz worker core (the host layout had not been updated
# for the second radiod).  Only this file was measured in the
# environment radiod runs in.
#
# Covers BOTH RX888 front-end rates: rof1620000 (64.8 Msps) and
# rof3240000 (129.6 Msps), the demod channel sizes and the 23 ka9q-web
# zoom levels.  Converged: /var/lib/ka9q-radio/fft.log stayed EMPTY
# across the restart that followed.
#
# At 129.6 Msps with 36-45 channels per radiod the fft thread sits at
# 85-100 % of a 3.2 GHz 5560U core with no sample loss; the plan does not
# buy headroom there, 64.8 Msps does.  Harvested from AI6VN-PM
# 2026-11-01.
